From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL DO NOT SUBMIT v4] drm/nouveau: preserve HDMI deep-colour GCP across audio enable

Hardware-discovery patch, revision 4, for the GA106 -> KDL-46HX855
controlled test. Includes everything from v3 (do not stack).

Run 4 proved the 12-bpc GCP value reached the SF register immediately
before the core-channel commit, but the instrumentation did not observe
the final state. The post-commit HDMI-audio enable path subsequently sends
SET_OD_PACKET with a legacy zero-depth GCP and overwrites GCP_SUBPACK with
0x10. That deterministically erases CD=6 and PP=2 after v3's readback.

NVIDIA's NVKMS performs the same legacy EnableHdmiAudio() operation, then
immediately calls SendHdmiGcp(), rebuilding CD/PP from the committed head
pixelDepth. Mirror that ordering on nouveau's GSP path: cache the requested
CD/PP when programming HDMI, then reconstruct the GCP from that state after
the audio RM calls while updating AVMUTE in SB0. Also make the primary GCP
writer update only SB0..SB2, matching NVIDIA's read-modify-write packet
routine, and log the post-audio GCP state.

This patch tests one source-proven clobber only. It does not yet add the
separate proprietary CTRL_HDMI call discovered behind SendHdmiGcp().

Base: Debian linux-source 7.0.10 tree, same as v1-v3 builds.
Applies with patch -p1.
